<x-legal-layout title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using CityCare Medical Centre's public website and patient portal.">
    <section id="acceptance">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">1. Using CityCare online services</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">These terms apply when you visit this website or use a CityCare account. By using the patient portal, you agree to follow these terms and the <a href="{{ route('legal.privacy') }}" class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline">Privacy policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not create or use an account.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">The website and portal support services provided by CityCare Medical Centre in Kampala, Uganda. They help patients and clinic staff manage information and service steps; they do not replace care from a qualified clinician.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="accounts">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">2. Patient accounts and account safety</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 ps-5">
            <li>Provide accurate details and keep your contact information current so the clinic can manage your account and visit.</li>
            <li>Keep your password and sign-in codes private. You are responsible for activity carried out using your account. Tell the clinic promptly if you believe someone else has accessed it.</li>
            <li>Use your own account. Do not impersonate another person, access records without permission, or attempt to bypass access controls.</li>
            <li>Staff accounts are for assigned clinic duties. Staff must only view or change information required for their work and must keep patient information confidential.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="care">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">3. Appointments and clinical care</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">The portal lets patients request or book available consultations and laboratory tests. A booking is subject to the schedule and confirmation shown by CityCare. Contact the clinic if you need to change or cancel a visit.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">Diagnosis, treatment, prescriptions, laboratory interpretation and decisions about whether you are ready to leave the clinic are made by the responsible care professionals. The portal displays and coordinates information; it does not provide emergency response or real-time medical advice. For urgent or emergency care, go to the nearest emergency facility.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">Patients should provide complete and truthful information relevant to their care. Do not use the portal to submit information on behalf of another adult unless you are authorized to do so.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="billing">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">4. Fees, online payments and receipts</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">Applicable consultation, laboratory and medication charges are shown by the clinic as separate bill items. Review the amount and currency before paying. The portal supports clinic-recorded payments and online checkout by available mobile money or card methods through PesaPal.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">Online checkout is handled by the payment provider. CityCare records the payment amount, reference and status returned for the transaction and makes receipts available for completed payments. Payment confirmation can take time to reach the portal; do not submit another payment for the same bill while a transaction is pending. Contact clinic staff if the status does not update or an amount appears incorrect.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">A payment receipt confirms a recorded transaction. It does not by itself confirm that a consultation, laboratory test, prescription or clinical clearance is complete. Any correction, cancellation or refund request should be raised with CityCare staff for review against the relevant visit and payment record.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="availability">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">5. Responsible use and availability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">Do not disrupt the service, upload harmful code, probe accounts or systems, or use another person's information without authority. CityCare may restrict or suspend access where necessary to protect patients, records, staff or the service.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">CityCare works to keep the website and portal available, but access may be interrupted for maintenance, connectivity, security or service-provider issues. If you cannot use the portal, contact the clinic through its usual in-person or communication channels.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="updates">
